    "show_share": true,
    "description": "One in four middle-aged adults in Pakistan is living with cardiovascular diseases which are the leading cause of death in the country. Even though men and women are equally susceptible to developing heart diseases, the risk of dying or becoming severely unwell due to heart disease is largely underestimated in women due to under-diagnosis and under-treatment, said speakers at the 2nd Annual Cardiovascular Conference Pulse 2021 held at Aga Khan University.",
